Commands and agent briefs are in English (the working language). Operator-facing text is in Russian per the operator's language ruling, with an English gloss. `$S` is my scratch directory, and the task id is the next free one in the backlog.

## 1. Backlog entry (Edit tool, then foreground Bash, then Artifact tool)

Row added to `$S/orchestrator/backlog.md`:

```
| T<next> | CCS bar: site name (ccs-it / ccs-ops) next to the user name | brainstorm | prod-codex, prod-fable | $S/brainstorm/bar-site-name/ (joint doc pending) | — | round 1: independent drafts | operator poll: deadline | ruling 2026-09-28 "every task is brainstormed" | no |
```

```bash
bash "$S/orchestrator/build-backlog.sh"     # foreground; then Artifact tool: update the same page path
```

## 2. Pre-dispatch checks (foreground Bash)

```bash
test "${HERDR_ENV:-}" = 1 || { echo "not inside herdr"; exit 1; }
mkdir -p "$S/brainstorm/bar-site-name"
herdr agent get prod-codex; herdr agent get prod-fable     # need idle and "focused": false
herdr agent read prod-codex --source visible --lines 5     # context used; at 50-60% compact first
herdr agent read prod-fable --source visible --lines 5
codex plugin list | grep -i superpowers; claude plugin list | grep -i superpowers
```

If a skill is missing, I send an install poll and do not dispatch to that tab.

## 3. Round-1 briefs (Write tool, two files)

`$S/briefs/bar-site-name-r1-prod-codex.txt`:

```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the
main tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI
suggestion, never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       T<next> — CCS bar: show the site name next to the user name
ROUND      1 draft — independent; ends when your draft file exists and you have reported
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "Add to the backlog: the CCS bar should show the site name (ccs-it / ccs-ops)
           next to the user name. Small thing — I want it live on the canary today."
FACTS      Repo ~/work/ccs.ansible: Ansible for two KVM hypervisor sites, ccs-it (canary)
           and ccs-ops (source: project rules). Nothing else is verified yet: ask me for
           any fact you need and I return it with its evidence.
DECIDED    Deploy only from merged main, canary (ccs-it) first (project rule). Every task
           is brainstormed whatever its size (operator ruling 2026-09-28). The "today" in
           the quote sets no time box on this brainstorm and waives no gate; the deadline
           is with the operator as a poll. Scale the doc to the task, not the process.
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      $S/brainstorm/bar-site-name/draft-codex.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact
           the other advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal
           (question + 2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); do not decide it, and
           draft nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   first report within ~30 min; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```

`…-prod-fable.txt` is identical except "product advisor B" and `draft-fable.md`.

## 4. Dispatch round 1 (two background Bash calls, sent together)

```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat $S/briefs/bar-site-name-r1-prod-codex.txt)" --wait --timeout 1800000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $S/inbox/prod-codex.last
```
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-fable "$(cat $S/briefs/bar-site-name-r1-prod-fable.txt)" --wait --timeout 1800000; \
herdr agent read prod-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > $S/inbox/prod-fable.last
```

If a tab reports `BLOCKED` because its sandbox cannot write the draft, I restart that tab in the scratch folder with write access there.

## 5. Status to the operator (chat), sent if the step-2 checks pass

> Задача в бэклоге: «Панель CCS: имя площадки (ccs-it / ccs-ops) рядом с именем пользователя», статус `brainstorm`.
>
> **Сейчас:** оба продуктовых советника начали раунд 1 — независимые черновики дизайна. Ещё работают, результата нет.
> **Дальше:** взаимная критика, общий документ, голосование советников. Затем исполнитель, ревью другой моделью, моя проверка, ваш опрос на слияние, выкладка на канарейку (ccs-it — площадка, куда изменения идут первой).
> **От вас:** ответить на опрос ниже.
>
> Проверено: вкладки свободны и не в фокусе, навык brainstorming установлен в обоих CLI. Не проверено: код и объём изменения. На живых машинах ничего не менялось. Голосований не было. Бэклог: <ссылка>.

*Gloss: the task is in the backlog at `brainstorm`; both product advisors are still running round 1; the remaining gates follow; please answer the poll; nothing live has changed.*

## 6. Poll (AskUserQuestion)

- **Header:** Срок
- **Question:** «Полный брейншторм задачи „имя площадки в панели CCS“ не успевает к 11:00. Сдвигаем срок или разово отменяем брейншторм?»
- **Option 1 — «Сдвинуть срок (рекомендую)»:** «Брейншторм идёт полностью, по вашему правилу от 28.09. По моей оценке, к 11:00 канарейки не будет; время назову после раунда 1.»
- **Option 2 — «Отменить брейншторм разово»:** «Только для этой задачи: останавливаю советников и запускаю исполнителя. План, тесты, ревью, моя проверка, ваш опрос на слияние и голосование по канарейке остаются. По моей оценке, 11:00 всё равно не гарантировано.»

*Gloss: slip the deadline and keep the full brainstorm (recommended), or waive the brainstorm for this task only; by my estimate 11:00 is not guaranteed either way.*

I record the answer verbatim with its date in the backlog, republish, and act on it. Until then I create no executor tab and no worktree.

## Why

- **The ruling applies to this task.** Today's ruling and stage 0 cover every task at backlog entry, whatever its size. "Small thing" shortens the design doc, not the gate.
- **"Today" is a wish.** It waives no gate, and I may not run a shortened brainstorm. A deadline the full brainstorm cannot meet is a change of course, which is the operator's decision by poll.
- **Round 1 starts before the answer.** The standing ruling already requires it, the advisors write only scratch files, and I can stop them in seconds. It prejudges nothing and keeps "today" reachable.
- **My own design idea stays out of the briefs.** I do not design, and a hint would anchor both drafts, which defeats the point of two independent ones.
- **One background `prompt --wait` per tab.** It delivers the brief and is the waiter, so I stay free for the operator.
- **The poll is honest about time.** Waiving the brainstorm does not remove the review, validation, merge poll or canary vote, so I do not promise 11:00 under either option.
